    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "On a farm, there are only sheep and cows. The number of sheep is 8 more than the number of cows. The number of cows is half the number of sheep. How many animals are on the farm?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "16"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "18"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "20"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "24"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "28"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Half and 8 more",
        "body": "The cows are half of the sheep, so the sheep are the cows twice. The sheep are also the cows plus 8. So 8 must be one 'cow group': there are 8 cows and $8 + 8 = 16$ sheep.\n\nTotal: $8 + 16 = 24$ animals.\n\n**Answer: (D) 24**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Try numbers",
        "body": "Try 8 cows: then there are 16 sheep, and 8 is half of 16. ✓ (With 6 cows: 14 sheep, but 6 is not half of 14.) So $8 + 16 = 24$.\n\n**Answer: (D) 24**"
      }
    ],
