        "text": "8"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "5"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "9"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "How much each change adds",
        "body": "Changing a red token: 1 token becomes 3, so she gets 2 more tokens. Changing a white token: 1 becomes 2, so 1 more token.\n\nTo end with few tokens she should change white tokens. She has only 1 white token. After changing it she has only red tokens, so the second change must be a red one (which gives 3 white). The third change can be a white one again.\n\n$4 + 1 + 2 + 1 = 8$ tokens.\n\n**Answer: (C) 8**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Try it out",
        "body": "Start: 3 red, 1 white (4 tokens).\n\n1. White → 2 red: 5 red (5 tokens).\n2. Red → 3 white: 4 red, 3 white (7 tokens).\n3. White → 2 red: 6 red, 2 white (8 tokens).\n\nThree white changes are impossible: after the first one she has no white token left. Using two red changes gives at least $4 + 2 + 2 + 1 = 9$. So 8 is the smallest.\n\n**Answer: (C) 8**"
      }
    ],
